SENTENCE : s.
Awen     : np                 = 'Awen'.
Butor    : np                 = 'Butor'.
Celeste  : np                 = 'Celeste'.
Likes    : np \ (s / np)      = lambda x : lambda y : (x,y) in likes.
Is       : np \ (s / adj)     = lambda x : lambda p : p(x).
Be       : np \ (s / adj)     = lambda x : lambda p : p(x).
Be       : s / adj            = lambda p : p('you').
Like     : s / np             = lambda x : ('you', x) in likes.
Like     : adj / np           = lambda x : lambda y : (y, x) in likes.
Happy    : adj                = lambda x : x in happy.
Sad      : adj                = lambda x : x in sad.
Confused : adj                = lambda x : x in confused.
And      : s \ (s / s)        = lambda x : lambda y : x and y.
And      : adj \ (adj / adj)  = lambda p : lambda q : lambda x : p(x) and q(x).
If       : s \ (s / s)        = lambda p : lambda q : (not p) or q.
Everyone : s / (np \ s)       = lambda p : all (p(x) for x in people).
Everyone : (s / np) \ s       = lambda p : all (p(x) for x in people).
Someone  : s / (np \ s)       = lambda p : any (p(x) for x in people).
Someone  : (s / np) \ s       = lambda p : any (p(x) for x in people).
Nobody	 : s / (np \ s)		  = lambda p : not any (p(x) for x in people).
Nobody	 : (s / np) \ s		  = lambda p : not any (p(x) for x in people).
Herself  : np = 'self'.
Himself  : np = 'self'.
Really      : (np \ s) / (np \ s) = lambda f : f.
Sometimes   : (np \ s) / (np \ s) = lambda f : f.
Deeply      : (np \ s) / (np \ s) = lambda f : f.
Especially  : (np \ s) / (np \ s) = lambda f : f.
Probably    : (np \ s) / (np \ s) = lambda f : f.
Who      : s / (np \ s)       = 'who'.
Not      : adj / adj          = lambda p : (lambda x : not p(x)).
Tell     : (s / s) / np       = 'tell'.
Me       : np                 = 'me'.
Only     : np / np            = 'only'.
Only     : (np \ s) / (np \ s)= 'only'.
Does     : s / s              = 'does'.
Like     : np \ (s / np)      = lambda x : lambda y : (x,y) in likes.
